# Exact decoding of JSON numbers

JSON numbers given for integers, decimals and money are read from their
literal text, never through a binary float.

```catala-metadata
declaration scope S:
  input i content integer
  input d content decimal
  input m content money

  output ri content integer
  output rd content decimal
  output rm content money

scope S:
  definition ri equals i
  definition rd equals d
  definition rm equals m
```

Beyond 2^53 and 12 significant digits:

```catala-test-cli
$ catala test-scope S --input {"i":9007199254740993,"d":1234567890123,"m":12.34} -F json
{"ri":"9007199254740993","rd":"1234567890123","rm":"12.34"}
```

Decimal fractions that have no exact binary representation:

```catala-test-cli
$ catala test-scope S --input {"i":0,"d":0.1,"m":0.29} -F json
{"ri":"0","rd":"1/10","rm":"0.29"}
```

```catala-test-cli
$ catala test-scope S --input {"i":-12,"d":-123456789.0123456789,"m":-12.34} -F json
{"ri":"-12","rd":"-1234567890123456789/10000000000","rm":"-12.34"}
```

Exponent notation:

```catala-test-cli
$ catala test-scope S --input {"i":1e3,"d":1.5E-3,"m":1.2e+3} -F json
{"ri":"1000","rd":"3/2000","rm":"1200.00"}
```

Integral values beyond the 63-bit native integers:

```catala-test-cli
$ catala test-scope S --input {"i":123456789012345678901234567890,"d":123456789012345678901234567890,"m":10000000000000000} -F json
{"ri":"123456789012345678901234567890","rd":"123456789012345678901234567890","rm":"10000000000000000.00"}
```

Numeric strings:

```catala-test-cli
$ catala test-scope S --input {"i":"-0012","d":"-1/3","m":"1.5e2"} -F json
{"ri":"-12","rd":"-1/3","rm":"150.00"}
```
